SUMMARY:Using Grok Bot to Recover Websites While I Sleep + 2026 Year-End R
 eview
DESCRIPTION:WordPress Lancaster\nThis month\, **Austin Ginder** will show 
 how he uses **Grok Bot**\, a team of AI routines\, to watch and repair Wor
 dPress sites overnight. Every 30 minutes\, a down-site watcher checks for 
 outages\, connects over SSH and works out what broke. When the cause is ba
 d code\, it fixes it and writes up what it changed. In its first nine days
  it patched about a dozen live sites\, mostly while Austin was asleep.\n\n
 **What we'll cover:**\n\n* How the watcher sorts an outage: fixable\, not 
 ours\, or hands off\n* The fix order: update\, roll back\, patch\, and dea
 ctivate only as a last resort\n* Real fixes from the past month\, includin
 g PHP 8 fatals\, a Gravity Forms class change and a disabled PHP function\
 n* The steps after every fix: back up\, purge cache\, confirm the site loa
 ds\, and log the change\n* Reviewing security signals the same way: an ove
 rnight run covered 226 findings across 206 sites\n* The guardrails\, what 
 it still gets wrong\, and why it runs on Austin's Mac for now\n\nAfter the
  talk we'll do a **year-end review**. We'll look back at what we covered i
 n 2026\, share what changed in our own WordPress work this year\, and coll
 ect ideas for topics and speakers for 2027.\n\nThis is our last meetup of 
 the year. We're skipping December and will be back on the regular schedule
  (third Thursday) on **January 21\, 2027**.\n\nPizza 🍕 and introduction
 s at 7pm.\n\n🗒️ About our location\n\n* Free parking in lot off of ma
 rket street. [See here for directions to The Candy Factory\, Warehouse D](
 https://goo.gl/maps/2NFNcZFxQC1qi8M66).
